fix(mlnode): inject Content-Type:application/json for header-less POSTs

Network DAPI (Go-http-client/1.1) sends JSON bodies to
/api/v1/inference/up and /api/v1/inference/pow/init/generate
without setting Content-Type. Pydantic v2, shipped with the
FastAPI/Starlette pin used by the vllm 0.20 base, requires
Content-Type:application/json to interpret the body as JSON;
without it the bytes are surfaced to model_validate as a
string value, producing 422 model_attributes_type
"Input should be a valid dictionary or object".

The vllm 0.15.1 base predates Pydantic v2 strictness, which is
why production mlnode-009 accepts the same DAPI request shape
unchanged and only the vllm 0.20 mlnode image hits the regression.

Add a tiny plain-ASGI ContentTypeInjector middleware that adds
Content-Type:application/json to POST /api/* requests when the
header is missing. Applied as outermost middleware so the header
is in scope before any downstream parsing.

Verified end-to-end on RTX PRO 6000 SE running vllm 0.20.0 PoC v2:
- POST /api/v1/inference/up (no Content-Type): 422 -> 200 OK
- POST /api/v1/inference/pow/init/generate (no Content-Type):
  body parses; reaches vLLM backend
- Live DAPI on network-002 transitions through inference/up,
  stop, and pow/init/generate cleanly; PoC v2 generation runs.

